cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. The code, the tests and
  the documentation were produced by AI agents (Anthropic's Claude) under the
  direction of Timothy Seifert. They have not yet been reviewed by a human
  mathematician; see the README for what is exact, what is computed modulo a
  prime, what is proved only in AI-written notes, and what is only computed.
title: "HodgeLociCI: Hodge loci of combinations of complete-intersection cycles in hypersurfaces"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Seifert
    given-names: Timothy
version: 0.1.3
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24455334
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/timseifer/HodgeLociCI"
keywords:
  - Hodge loci
  - Noether-Lefschetz loci
  - linear cycles
  - complete-intersection cycles
  - hypersurfaces
  - Jacobian ring
  - Hilbert function
  - second-order obstruction
  - Fermat variety
  - Macaulay2
abstract: >-
  A Macaulay2 package for Hodge loci of classes r[Y1] + s[Y2] of two
  complete-intersection cycles in a smooth hypersurface of even dimension: a
  degree-level calculator for the first-order excess of the Hodge locus over
  the locus where both cycles persist, a second-order obstruction check at
  random or user-supplied points, and higher-order expansions at the Fermat
  point by pole-order reduction, with a validation suite against published
  numbers and a folder of Lean certificates. AI-generated; not yet reviewed
  by a human.
